  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Colophon information printed on library checkout card in pocket attached to page 3 of cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Materials: paper, watercolor, digital printing, bookboard, bookcloth.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1="1" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Jen Library's Special Collections copy is numbered 17 of 18 and is initialed by the artist. ACA Library copy edition 18 of 18.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Scenes from a daily journal of my commute by bus, bike and BART from Oakland to San Francisco and back in 2012"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Handset type, photo polymer plates, watercolor and inkjet on Rives BFK, Canson Mi-Tientes. Hand cut and bound in carousel format, with slipcase. Printed on the Vandercook SP20 at Kala Art Institute"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Drawings of commuters are letterpress printed, hand colored and cut and layered over a phone photo ... The five vignettes frame views through a bus window with a journal entry for each day of the work week"--Quite Contrary Press website, viewed on April 2, 2015.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Single opening carousel structure (a cross between pop-up and tunnel book) with five spreads, each with three layers of overlapping accordion folds with sections cut out to create a three-dimensional scene. When opened and magnetized covers are placed against each other, it forms a star-shaped structure, 10" in diameter. Images of street signs reading "Market" tipped in on the front and back boards. Slip case has tipped-in, letterpress printed spine label with title and author's initials.</subfield>
  </datafield>
